  "description": {
    "text": "The Shogakukan Ten Magazines Pokémon Card Game Design Contest (小学館10誌連合 ポケモンカードゲーム デザインコンテスト) of 2010 asked children to draw Zorua and Zoroark, the new Pokémon of that summer's film, Zoroark: Master of Illusions; entries closed by 24 April 2010, and the results appeared in the magazines' July 2010 issues. Judges including Tsunekazu Ishihara and the film's director, Kunihiko Yuyama, chose one grand prize winner for each magazine, whose work was shown at the start of the film and made into a card for them as a set of 100 copies, marked ポケモンカードゲーム デザインコンテスト 最優秀賞 (grand prize): ten cards, six of Zorua and four of Zoroark. A collector recalls that these turned up more often than the 2009 contest's, as one auction seller sold many full sets after the contest.",
